{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789254278,"nonce":"nuzoJA9FCGscdJ1Dl7/k8Q7ZCeA=","title":"zypy compiles every library function with Cranelift on each run","message":"The tiered runtime compiles every function in the module; the\nCranelift backend can skip bodies outside a reachable set\n(`set_only_compile_reachable`, `reachable_function_ids`), and the\nclassic and interpreter runtimes use it, but the tiered runtime never\nsets it. zypy knows its entry (`zyntax_python::ENTRY`) and its\nindirect calls are `FuncRef`s the reachability walk follows, so it can\nopt in: compute the set after optimisation, pass it to the backend,\nand codegen shrinks from the library to what the program reaches.\n\nMust stay opt-in per host: a host that calls arbitrary functions with\n`call_raw` needs every body.","files":null}]}